1
00:00:09,261 --> 00:00:12,740
A body is left in a small
room in eastern Tibet.

2
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:14,670
Over a week it grows smaller.

3
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:16,789
Rainbows are seen above the roof.

4
00:00:16,869 --> 00:00:20,761
When the door is opened,
only hair and nails remain.

5
00:00:21,604 --> 00:00:24,377
Four papers tell this
story. They tell it well.

6
00:00:24,457 --> 00:00:28,345
They also tell it in a way that can
quietly bring back the very thing the

7
00:00:28,425 --> 00:00:30,835
story is meant to free us from.

8
00:00:31,637 --> 00:00:36,720
This is After Anatta: notes by
John Tan, known as Thusness.

9
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:40,864
In this video we read four outside
papers on the rainbow body,

10
00:00:40,944 --> 00:00:44,491
light and the five elements.
We keep what holds.

11
00:00:44,571 --> 00:00:48,246
And we look closely at three
places where each of them slips.

12
00:00:49,078 --> 00:00:51,539
The four papers come
from different angles.

13
00:00:51,619 --> 00:00:55,506
One is an essay on light and
mind in Bön and Dzogchen.

14
00:00:55,586 --> 00:00:59,501
Bön is the old religion of
Tibet, with its own Dzogchen.

15
00:00:59,581 --> 00:01:03,387
One is a scholarly comparison
of light across three systems:

16
00:01:03,467 --> 00:01:07,069
Kālacakra, Nyingma Dzogchen, and Bön.

17
00:01:07,149 --> 00:01:10,955
One is a report on Bön practices
with the five elements.

18
00:01:11,035 --> 00:01:13,976
And one is a beginner's
guide to the rainbow body.

19
00:01:14,827 --> 00:01:16,527
First, what they report.

20
00:01:16,607 --> 00:01:18,243
And here they are mostly right.

21
00:01:19,049 --> 00:01:23,996
In Dzogchen and in Bön, the rainbow
body is said to come at death.

22
00:01:24,076 --> 00:01:26,550
Over several days the body shrinks.

23
00:01:26,630 --> 00:01:28,507
Sweet scents replace decay.

24
00:01:28,587 --> 00:01:31,170
Rainbows and beams of light appear.

25
00:01:31,250 --> 00:01:34,118
In the end only hair and nails are left.

26
00:01:34,198 --> 00:01:39,539
A rarer kind, the great transference,
is said to need no death at all.

27
00:01:39,619 --> 00:01:42,393
The body itself becomes a body of light.

28
00:01:42,473 --> 00:01:46,487
The tradition names
Padmasambhava and Vimalamitra.

29
00:01:47,314 --> 00:01:49,286
The papers also give the path.

30
00:01:49,366 --> 00:01:52,017
In Dzogchen there are two practices.

31
00:01:52,097 --> 00:01:56,732
Cutting through means recognising the
knowing that is empty and clear at once,

32
00:01:56,812 --> 00:02:01,161
and resting in it. Direct crossing
works with the display itself.

33
00:02:01,241 --> 00:02:06,052
With certain postures and gazes,
lights appear in open space.

34
00:02:06,132 --> 00:02:07,673
Small drops of light.

35
00:02:07,776 --> 00:02:12,696
Fine threads. They grow into patterns,
and then into whole mandalas.

36
00:02:12,776 --> 00:02:15,223
The texts call these the four visions.

37
00:02:15,303 --> 00:02:18,570
The fourth is called the
exhaustion of phenomena.

38
00:02:19,406 --> 00:02:21,718
The texts also speak of lamps.

39
00:02:21,798 --> 00:02:23,674
One lamp is the eyes.

40
00:02:23,754 --> 00:02:26,853
Another is the open sky
the lights appear in.

41
00:02:26,933 --> 00:02:29,598
Another is the circles
of light themselves.

42
00:02:29,678 --> 00:02:33,552
And the last is the wisdom that
knows them as its own display.

43
00:02:33,632 --> 00:02:36,215
The lights do not appear
apart from seeing.

44
00:02:36,295 --> 00:02:38,407
They are seeing, recognised.

45
00:02:39,221 --> 00:02:42,719
So far, good reporting.
Now the three slips.

46
00:02:43,534 --> 00:02:47,141
The first slip is the biggest.
Light becomes a stuff.

47
00:02:47,954 --> 00:02:52,073
The papers say that light is the
building block of the cosmos.

48
00:02:52,153 --> 00:02:54,274
That matter is light condensed.

49
00:02:54,354 --> 00:02:57,603
That the solid world is
a collapse of open space,

50
00:02:57,683 --> 00:03:00,116
cooling and hardening like ice.

51
00:03:00,196 --> 00:03:04,618
One of them says that awareness is
the space in which the light plays.

52
00:03:05,417 --> 00:03:07,932
It sounds deep. But follow it through.

53
00:03:08,012 --> 00:03:12,565
If light is what everything is made
of, then light is one more ground.

54
00:03:12,645 --> 00:03:15,731
A finer substance,
shining instead of solid,

55
00:03:15,811 --> 00:03:18,040
but a substance all the same.

56
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:20,649
And if awareness is the space it plays in,

57
00:03:20,729 --> 00:03:22,868
then awareness is a container.

58
00:03:23,685 --> 00:03:26,050
Dzogchen itself does not need this.

59
00:03:26,130 --> 00:03:28,211
Its ground has three aspects.

60
00:03:28,291 --> 00:03:32,029
Its essence is empty,
pure from the beginning.

61
00:03:32,109 --> 00:03:35,493
Its nature is clear,
spontaneously present.

62
00:03:35,573 --> 00:03:37,572
And its display never stops.

63
00:03:37,652 --> 00:03:40,928
Hold the first one in view,
and the picture changes.

64
00:03:41,008 --> 00:03:43,890
The five lights are display
with nothing behind them.

65
00:03:43,970 --> 00:03:46,571
They do not condense
out of a shining stuff.

66
00:03:47,390 --> 00:03:52,052
Then what do the texts mean when they
say the lights harden into the elements?

67
00:03:52,132 --> 00:03:55,354
Read with care, it names
how appearing is taken.

68
00:03:55,434 --> 00:03:59,837
When the display is not recognised,
it is grasped as something other,

69
00:03:59,917 --> 00:04:04,905
standing over there. That grasping is
what makes the elements seem solid.

70
00:04:04,985 --> 00:04:08,030
Nothing turned solid.
Nothing was ever frozen.

71
00:04:08,110 --> 00:04:12,817
There was only a deep habit of seeing
things as if they stood by themselves.

72
00:04:13,637 --> 00:04:18,557
Try it now with something in your hand.
An apple, a cup. There is hardness.

73
00:04:18,637 --> 00:04:20,921
There is coolness. There is colour.

74
00:04:21,001 --> 00:04:23,190
Each appears as its conditions meet.

75
00:04:23,270 --> 00:04:26,292
Then habit ties them into one solid thing,

76
00:04:26,422 --> 00:04:30,418
out there, as if they all
belonged to a core underneath.

77
00:04:30,498 --> 00:04:34,549
That knot is the hardening.
Untie it, and nothing is lost.

78
00:04:34,629 --> 00:04:38,638
The hardness, the red, the
coolness are all still here.

79
00:04:38,718 --> 00:04:41,020
Only the extra solidity drops.

80
00:04:41,841 --> 00:04:44,356
This is also how to
read the fourth vision.

81
00:04:44,436 --> 00:04:49,410
The papers say that everything dissolves
back into primordial emptiness.

82
00:04:49,490 --> 00:04:52,440
As if emptiness were a
place things return to.

83
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:55,701
But emptiness is not a
place, and not a source.

84
00:04:55,781 --> 00:05:00,416
What is used up in the exhaustion of
phenomena is the holding of appearances as

85
00:05:00,496 --> 00:05:02,603
things with a nature of their own.

86
00:05:02,683 --> 00:05:05,148
Appearing itself is not wiped out.

87
00:05:05,978 --> 00:05:09,241
The same care is needed
with light inside the body.

88
00:05:09,321 --> 00:05:13,833
One paper says the heart is a
vessel that holds a radiant mandala,

89
00:05:13,913 --> 00:05:19,913
waiting to break out. The tradition does
use that image: a youthful body in a vase.

90
00:05:20,136 --> 00:05:25,355
But it is a simile. Taken literally, it
is a light stored inside a container.

91
00:05:25,435 --> 00:05:29,784
In John Tan's reading, clarity
is never stored anywhere.

92
00:05:29,864 --> 00:05:32,814
It is the knowing clarity
of appearing itself,

93
00:05:32,894 --> 00:05:36,079
and it is as empty as whatever appears.

94
00:05:36,881 --> 00:05:38,988
So the first correction is simple.

95
00:05:39,068 --> 00:05:42,630
Light names how appearing
shines when it is not grasped.

96
00:05:42,710 --> 00:05:44,794
It is not what the world is made of.

97
00:05:45,610 --> 00:05:47,528
The second slip is quieter.

98
00:05:47,608 --> 00:05:49,448
Reports become facts.

99
00:05:50,270 --> 00:05:53,247
The papers say the rainbow body is proven.

100
00:05:53,327 --> 00:05:55,747
That hundreds of witnesses verified it.

101
00:05:55,827 --> 00:05:59,525
That it is physical,
empirical proof of liberation.

102
00:05:59,605 --> 00:06:03,641
They list cases with dates,
some going back many centuries,

103
00:06:03,721 --> 00:06:06,254
some as recent as the last few years.

104
00:06:07,074 --> 00:06:11,057
Here we have to be honest. These
are reports. Some are moving.

105
00:06:11,137 --> 00:06:12,973
Some come from people who were there.

106
00:06:13,053 --> 00:06:15,826
But none has been checked
by anyone independent.

107
00:06:15,906 --> 00:06:19,553
And when the lists are looked at
closely, they do not all hold.

108
00:06:20,374 --> 00:06:24,357
One famous master is listed
as a rainbow body case,

109
00:06:24,437 --> 00:06:28,419
though his body was ordinary at
death and his relics were kept.

110
00:06:28,499 --> 00:06:33,297
Another master's death is dated to one
year in one source and seventeen years

111
00:06:33,377 --> 00:06:37,713
later in another. The sixteenth
Karmapa is listed too.

112
00:06:37,793 --> 00:06:42,251
But what was reported after his
death is tukdam, not a rainbow body.

113
00:06:42,331 --> 00:06:47,713
Tukdam is a state in which a practitioner
is said to rest in meditation after death.

114
00:06:47,793 --> 00:06:53,270
The body stays fresh, and warm at the
heart, for days. It does not shrink.

115
00:06:53,350 --> 00:06:54,710
It does not vanish.

116
00:06:54,790 --> 00:07:00,790
In 2021, a team from the University of
Wisconsin measured thirteen such cases.

117
00:07:01,026 --> 00:07:03,080
They found no brain activity.

118
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:06,925
But they could only begin recording
a day or more after death,

119
00:07:07,005 --> 00:07:08,709
so the question stays open.

120
00:07:09,517 --> 00:07:14,641
And the most often told modern
case, Khenpo A Chö in 1998,

121
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:17,643
rests on eyewitness accounts
gathered afterwards,

122
00:07:17,723 --> 00:07:21,937
and on a local press report that the
body shrank to the size of a bean.

123
00:07:22,017 --> 00:07:26,230
A priest and scholar, Francis
Tiso, went to look into it.

124
00:07:26,310 --> 00:07:28,558
What he could gather was
what people told him.

125
00:07:29,369 --> 00:07:31,992
None of this says the reports are false.

126
00:07:32,072 --> 00:07:33,886
It says what kind of thing they are.

127
00:07:34,701 --> 00:07:36,835
And it matters less than it seems.

128
00:07:36,915 --> 00:07:41,455
Within Dzogchen itself, teachers warn
against taking the shrinking body for the

129
00:07:41,535 --> 00:07:45,721
rainbow body. The rainbow
body is first a realization.

130
00:07:45,801 --> 00:07:48,833
When the fourth vision
is complete, everything,

131
00:07:48,913 --> 00:07:53,425
the body included, is seen as
the display of the five lights.

132
00:07:53,505 --> 00:07:55,708
That seeing is the rainbow body.

133
00:07:55,788 --> 00:07:58,615
What happens to the corpse
is at most a sign of it,

134
00:07:58,695 --> 00:08:00,490
and not always a sign at all.

135
00:08:00,570 --> 00:08:05,572
Some teachers call a body that shrinks
and disappears a partial rainbow body.

136
00:08:05,652 --> 00:08:08,266
A sign that the work
was not quite finished.

137
00:08:09,086 --> 00:08:12,716
So the second correction:
keep the reports as reports.

138
00:08:12,796 --> 00:08:15,166
The realization does not wait on them.

139
00:08:15,978 --> 00:08:19,666
The third slip is about
traditions. Three become one.

140
00:08:20,508 --> 00:08:26,094
The papers put Kālacakra, Nyingma
Dzogchen and Bön into one table,

141
00:08:26,174 --> 00:08:30,455
as if they were one system with
three names. They share words.

142
00:08:30,535 --> 00:08:33,607
Light, drops, channels, winds.

143
00:08:33,687 --> 00:08:35,405
But they are not the same path.

144
00:08:36,229 --> 00:08:38,880
Kālacakra speaks of empty form.

145
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:42,942
In its night and day
yogas, vivid images appear:

146
00:08:43,022 --> 00:08:47,793
smoke, a mirage,
fireflies, a lamp, a flame,

147
00:08:47,873 --> 00:08:53,391
the moon, the sun, darkness,
lightning, a great drop of light.

148
00:08:53,471 --> 00:08:56,964
Its texts say these images
are made of no atoms at all.

149
00:08:57,044 --> 00:09:00,755
They go beyond existence
and beyond non-existence.

150
00:09:00,835 --> 00:09:05,673
They are compared to the image a young
girl sees in a divining mirror. Vivid.

151
00:09:05,753 --> 00:09:08,436
Clear. And nothing behind the glass.

152
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:12,927
This is the most beautiful
line in all four papers.

153
00:09:13,007 --> 00:09:18,647
The Italian scholar Giacomella Orofino
traces it in her study of light in the

154
00:09:18,727 --> 00:09:21,976
tantras. And it fits
the view here closely.

155
00:09:22,056 --> 00:09:25,064
What appears is vivid,
and it is not found.

156
00:09:25,882 --> 00:09:29,376
But Kālacakra's goal is
not the rainbow body.

157
00:09:29,456 --> 00:09:34,090
It speaks of a union of empty
form and unchanging bliss.

158
00:09:34,170 --> 00:09:37,392
The word for that is
union, not body of light.

159
00:09:37,472 --> 00:09:41,214
Joining the two makes a
neat table, and loses both.

160
00:09:42,038 --> 00:09:47,393
Bön, in turn, has its own Dzogchen,
its own lamps and visions,

161
00:09:47,473 --> 00:09:49,336
and its own rainbow body.

162
00:09:49,416 --> 00:09:53,466
One of its great masters,
Shardza Tashi Gyaltsen,

163
00:09:53,546 --> 00:09:56,496
is said to have attained it in 1934.

164
00:09:56,576 --> 00:10:00,803
Bön also has rituals that Buddhism
does not frame the same way.

165
00:10:00,883 --> 00:10:03,711
The four guests, who receive offerings.

166
00:10:03,791 --> 00:10:08,118
A dough shaped in the hand and
offered to beings one owes a debt to.

167
00:10:08,933 --> 00:10:11,081
Even the tables of colours shift.

168
00:10:11,161 --> 00:10:14,817
Which element goes with
which Buddha, which wisdom,

169
00:10:14,897 --> 00:10:18,282
which poison: these
differ from text to text.

170
00:10:18,362 --> 00:10:21,407
Any single table is one lineage's pairing.

171
00:10:21,487 --> 00:10:23,336
It is a map for practice.

172
00:10:23,416 --> 00:10:26,031
It is not a chart of what
the world is made of.

173
00:10:26,841 --> 00:10:31,453
So the third correction: let each
tradition speak in its own voice.

174
00:10:32,282 --> 00:10:34,254
One more caution belongs here.

175
00:10:34,334 --> 00:10:39,009
One paper presents the Bön element
practices as a plan for health and even

176
00:10:39,089 --> 00:10:43,479
for mental health. That they draw
illness and trauma out of the body.

177
00:10:43,559 --> 00:10:45,422
Nothing like this has been tested.

178
00:10:45,502 --> 00:10:47,501
These are spiritual practices.

179
00:10:47,581 --> 00:10:50,844
They do not replace a
doctor, or care for the mind.

180
00:10:50,924 --> 00:10:54,539
And forced breathing, or trying
to stay awake through sleep,

181
00:10:54,619 --> 00:10:58,181
has left some practitioners
sleepless and unsettled.

182
00:10:58,261 --> 00:11:00,957
Such practices need a qualified teacher.

183
00:11:01,782 --> 00:11:07,015
There is one more thing the papers carry,
and it is worth keeping. A Tibetan image.

184
00:11:07,095 --> 00:11:12,395
Raw leather is stiff. Rub butter into
it under the sun, and it grows soft.

185
00:11:12,475 --> 00:11:15,208
But a leather bag used
only to store butter,

186
00:11:15,288 --> 00:11:18,441
year after year, slowly hardens like wood.

187
00:11:18,521 --> 00:11:20,697
Then no butter will soften it again.

188
00:11:20,777 --> 00:11:25,144
Knowledge never rubbed in by
practice does the same. It hardens.

189
00:11:25,978 --> 00:11:28,942
That may be the best way
to read these four papers.

190
00:11:29,022 --> 00:11:32,723
Not as facts to store, but
as an invitation to look.

191
00:11:33,529 --> 00:11:35,287
So, what turns into light?

192
00:11:36,101 --> 00:11:39,186
Read with emptiness, the answer is quiet.

193
00:11:39,266 --> 00:11:41,632
Nothing found turns into light.

194
00:11:41,712 --> 00:11:44,363
The body appeared solid
because it was held.

195
00:11:44,443 --> 00:11:49,214
When the holding ends, it no longer
appears so. Nothing is produced.

196
00:11:49,294 --> 00:11:54,540
Nothing is lost. The same hardness,
the same warmth, the same colour,

197
00:11:54,620 --> 00:11:57,493
vivid and appearing as
their conditions meet.

198
00:11:58,305 --> 00:12:01,961
That is why the rainbow body
is not the measure of insight.

199
00:12:02,041 --> 00:12:03,877
And it is not a goal to aim at.

200
00:12:03,957 --> 00:12:08,161
To practise for a body of light is
still to practise for something.

201
00:12:08,978 --> 00:12:11,507
The lights were never a
stuff behind the world.

202
00:12:11,587 --> 00:12:14,487
They were the world,
seen without grasping.

